{
  "_comment": [
    "Retrieval ground truth. Each question names the documents that could",
    "honestly answer it, by source_id.",
    "",
    "`expect` is a set rather than a single id because several concepts are",
    "spread across genuinely interchangeable documents -- OpenDSA splits",
    "hashing across nine files, and a question about collisions is answered",
    "correctly by any of three. The sets are kept tight: a document is in",
    "one only if a passage from it would actually let the critic say",
    "something specific and true about the question.",
    "",
    "The earlier version of this set matched on repository prefix",
    "('cpython:', 'opendsa:'), which with the concept filter already applied",
    "was nearly free and made the hit rate look better than it was. These",
    "are document-level.",
    "",
    "`concept` is the tag the filtered run scopes to. The unfiltered run",
    "ignores it, which is the harder measurement: it says whether the",
    "embeddings are doing the work or the metadata is."
  ],
